      "writtenOn": "2020-12-14T18:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should the solution be at the extpower_is_present() level then?  Currently, it\u0027s defined as:\n\n* Return non-zero if external power is present.\n\nin include/extpower.h.  I feel like we should have clear API expectations here as to what can return just \"non-zero\" and what specifically is expecting a 1 (though I defer to you as the EC core owner :) )",
      "parentUuid": "3fd1fbbe_71dd16cd",
      "revId": "f1c69f9f3da12a0a647f2bbb2b5670b5ed3399f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
